/forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T11:42:43-07:00","id":1513960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513762-sorcerous-societies-new-revised-sects-orders#post1513762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...in early 1e, we had a very clear division- mages were either a Pentacle or a Seer. Easy and simple. However, as the setting evolved and developed, things became much less easy to define- the Pentacle was a modern creation from the get go, and the separation between the Diamond and the Free Council became more and more apparent as time progressed...</div> </div> </div> </div>Making them a sect kinda just recognised the weirdness of the 1e structure; like early 1e really makes a big deal of the fact that the Diamond barely tolerates the FC. 2e (and latterly 1e) makes the Pentacle a much more cooperative alliance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After all, the Diamond Orders have their own Factions, very different ideologies and do not always work together in harmony. What does it take for a Order to become a Sect is a question that has been bugging me for a while, and that I plan on trying to answer for myself in here. </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty good idea. As I understand it, the FC were written to cover two separable roles that the writers wanted covered; ie. 'technomages' and 'cultural' mages that stick much closer to specific sleeper cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T15:41:07-07:00","id":1513975,"title":"","content":"So while I originally planned on this project to be mostly my rumbling and bits and pieces of useful stuff, it seems like it started to coalesce into a more defined form, with some actual mechanics up there! Currently I've finished the revised Diamond, and the next step will be to rebuild the Guardians and the Mysterium as their own Sects. I have considered to also break the Arrow apart, but I couldn't think of a better representation of Fortitude in the revised paradigm. You can find the current material <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1a5eO3BAN5J_wA9qPy__kTlL9LU5OKptZIx_Q2XZXtOY/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">in here</a>. Feel free to let me know what do you think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T17:45:07-07:00","id":1514068,"title":"","content":"I feel the need to point out that the unifying element of the Diamond sect is the Elemental Precept &quot;The Awakened are One Nation&quot;, also known as the Diamond Precept. The Silver Ladder lobbied hard for that and the Seers are notably lesser in numbers than the Pentacle. The Diamond Orders weren't called that because there are 4 sides to the shape, but because the fundamental shared/agreed upon concept (that we can do this better if we work together as our own society) was associated with the gemstone in the philosophy of it's most vocal advocates.<br /> I say this because the first section (&quot;Broken Diamond&quot;) spends a lot of time kind of missing that point.<br /> Yes, from a meta standpoint, the Diamond was about the 4 orders making it up...but it was from a meta standpoint that no longer applies with the newer source material. At the very least, it was untrue by the time 2nd edition came out. It means something else now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, what stops the Silver Ladder, the Guardians and the Arrow from breaking apart?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silver Ladder spends more time than it likes making sure they don't break apart. Heck, I'm pretty sure <b>Consilia</b>\u200b exist to lessen the pressure to just run off and never talk to one another again. which is why the Pentacle recognizes Assemblies as Consilia with a different structure. Because they exist to keep the peace and channels of communication open. Knowing this, in my opinion, is kind of required to running the Silver Ladder in games. In this alternate setting, they failed to hold on to either of the Mysterium's foundational Orders after the Corpus Mysteriorum began circulating, if I am seeing where you are going with this.<br /> <br /> Another concern I have before I hit the next section is that you mention the &quot;dragon&quot; element of the Orders as Atlantean...but in Tome of the Pentacle, it officially came out that was an element the Tremere contributed to the Diamond during their tenure as members. I feel the need to point out that the Orders are constructs of Fallen World history and direct heirs of physical Atlantis. They arose When Great Cults met and people saw their teachings, mysteries and Truths mirrored amongst strangers. Then time passes and new ideas circulate, building them up little by little. They don't spring fully formed from the Time Before anymore.<br /> <br /> Now the concept of &quot;Mages are the embodiment of Truth&quot; as Atlantean...Atlantis is much more divorced from the reality in 2nd ed. It exists as philosophic stand-in for what was lost in the Fall. It never existed in their timeline, and the times it did, it probably wasn't called Atlantis, (or Shangri-La, Ubar, Irem or any of the other names that the Mage line has called it over the years). Atlantean is not a single definition, <b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple </b>spends a lot of wordcount explaining that very well.<br /> I think the word you're looking for is Supernal. Because claiming that magical symbolism comes from a common &quot;ancestral&quot; culture that developed under the divine realms of Truth, is a LOT easier to sell to other such groups if you agree ALL the names are a little wrong. The Supernal Realms are a common enough touchstone to work in that regard. Especially when the argument is &quot;we are all expressions of the same Truth, let's compare notes and work together&quot;.<br /> To be clear, it is less that statement I disagree with, and more the idea that the Orders tie themselves so strongly to &quot;Atlantis&quot; as a name.<br /> <br /> Honestly the fact that you tie the Orders to virtues in a bizarre, twisted fashion of Plato-inspired philosophy...works rather well for Mage, with it's pseudo-imperialism and patronizing separation of Sleeper beliefs and Awakened practices. This I can get behind. Justified nonsense is exactly the kind of thing I expect to see in a game about wizards with freeform magic and any half decent framework can generate interesting ideas here. If this is how they wishes to sell the Diamond Precept in this setting, I can buy it.<br /> <br /> The Atlantean Diamond is next, but not right now.<br /> <br /> Edit: I forgot goal <b>7 (Welcome to Atlantis)</b>, which is much closer to 1st ed's interpretation of the Fallen World, but I'm going to let my previous statements stand because they did make up a lot of how I viewed this section. I still feel my perspective had merit, even if it was misaligned with the intentions of the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-06-2023, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T23:00:19-07:00","id":1514078,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> I am yet to able able to respond in detail for your points, but I just wanted to point out that when I discussed the idea of Atlantis in here, I didn't mean &quot;Atlantis as a place&quot; but &quot;Atlantis as a symbol&quot;. I use the term here to refer to &quot;an Awakened, utopian Society&quot; (obviously there are other terms, but I thought that at least for the Diamond themselves it would be fitting to be put in the title. Of course, opinions may vary and I am fine with just calling them &quot;the Diamond&quot;). In this setting, it is a &quot;modern&quot; term that the Ladder sometimes uses in order to enforce unity within their society. I used the term &quot;Dragon&quot; in here because we have &quot;parts of the Dragon&quot; for every Order which was part of the Diamond *modern ones and Lost ones), and it probably was embraced (and still maintained) due to the way it reinforces a sense of unity in an otherwise very different Orders.<br /> <br /> So in my mind, in Atlantis is still a metaphor/symbol and the Dragon is still a later addition made by the Tremere, if it helps your concerns about this subject. Welcome to Atlantis is a but of a curveball in that regards. Things will get funky with this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T05:11:32-07:00","id":1514108,"title":"","content":"The Core Belief and Symbolism of the Forge of Vulcan and Watchers of Fortune in detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","user":"Phoenix853457","date":". 06-07-2023, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T13:58:15-07:00","id":1514128,"title":"","content":"So a bit more deep response-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513762-sorcerous-societies-new-revised-sects-orders?p=1514068#post1514068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the need to point out that the unifying element of the Diamond sect is the Elemental Precept &quot;The Awakened are One Nation&quot;, also known as the Diamond Precept. The Silver Ladder lobbied hard for that and the Seers are notably lesser in numbers than the Pentacle. The Diamond Orders weren't called that because there are 4 sides to the shape, but because the fundamental shared/agreed upon concept (that we can do this better if we work together as our own society) was associated with the gemstone in the philosophy of it's most vocal advocates.<br /> I say this because the first section (&quot;Broken Diamond&quot;) spends a lot of time kind of missing that point.<br /> Yes, from a meta standpoint, the Diamond was about the 4 orders making it up...but it was from a meta standpoint that no longer applies with the newer source material. At the very least, it was untrue by the time 2nd edition came out. It means something else now.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silver Ladder being the main entity that drives the Diamond is something that I hope I addressed in the writeup, and I fully agrre with that principle. The point about the Diamond is a bit of an issue for me for some meta reasons- in 1e, I am pretty sure that the Diamond were called the Diamond because that there were 4 Orders, hence why when the Free Council joined it was renamed the Pentacle. Sure, 2e have added its own explanation for it, but honestly I am not a fan of names simply being carried over when the context which produced them is no longer relevant (I am looking at you, Disciplines and Glamour). Also, I do refer to how historically we can see consistent pattern of those four emerging (To the Strongest and Mutapa), and we do know that the Orders are part of the Supernal Symbols, so I do tend to give that concept of &quot;four-fold Diamond&quot; some significance (perhaps some more than I should have, but still).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another concern I have before I hit the next section is that you mention the &quot;dragon&quot; element of the Orders as Atlantean...but in Tome of the Pentacle, it officially came out that was an element the Tremere contributed to the Diamond during their tenure as members. I feel the need to point out that the Orders are constructs of Fallen World history and direct heirs of physical Atlantis. They arose When Great Cults met and people saw their teachings, mysteries and Truths mirrored amongst strangers. Then time passes and new ideas circulate, building them up little by little. They don't spring fully formed from the Time Before anymore. </div> </div> </div>Point of clarity from my part. I referred to the Dragon because all Orders associated with the Dragon have, had one point, being considered a part of the &quot;Dragon&quot;. The Dragon is treated as a part of a &quot;greater whole&quot;, and it is &quot;Atlantean&quot; by the idea that it produces a sense of unification. Yes, the Tremere have been the ones who came up with that association, but the Diamond embraced it and maintained it because it has some Truth in it. As I mentioned in the earlier post, throughout the writeup I have not considered Atlantis as a physical place or the Orders simply descending from it, but instead have used the term to refer to the &quot;Symbol of an Awakened Utopia&quot; that failed. Being &quot;Atlantean&quot; in that regard is &quot;desiring a unified, Awakened society&quot;, which is what the Diamond aspires to be. So yeah, I also don't claim that the Orders directly descended fully formed from a Time Before- but I do claim that their symbols are part of the Supernal, and that the Orders were destined to emerge in the Fallen because of it (which I think is canon).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now the concept of &quot;Mages are the embodiment of Truth&quot; as Atlantean...Atlantis is much more divorced from the reality in 2nd ed. It exists as philosophic stand-in for what was lost in the Fall. It never existed in their timeline, and the times it did, it probably wasn't called Atlantis, (or Shangri-La, Ubar, Irem or any of the other names that the Mage line has called it over the years). Atlantean is not a single definition, <b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple </b>spends a lot of wordcount explaining that very well.<br /> I think the word you're looking for is Supernal. Because claiming that magical symbolism comes from a common &quot;ancestral&quot; culture that developed under the divine realms of Truth, is a LOT easier to sell to other such groups if you agree ALL the names are a little wrong. The Supernal Realms are a common enough touchstone to work in that regard. Especially when the argument is &quot;we are all expressions of the same Truth, let's compare notes and work together&quot;.<br /> To be clear, it is less that statement I disagree with, and more the idea that the Orders tie themselves so strongly to &quot;Atlantis&quot; as a name. </div> </div> </div>Again, everything written in the &quot;meta&quot; section is not to be taken as IC world view. I used Atlantis as a manner to avoid written &quot;Time Before&quot; and &quot;Awakened Utopia&quot; too many times. It is shorter and (I believed) delivered the point that I use it symbolically. Apparently, that didn't passed and I'll try to be clearer next time. This is why during the IC sections I have tried to minimize the use of the word Atlantis, except in the Diamond's title (again, with it being a symbol of the utopia and a sign of their vision, not an actual place or event) and the Exemplars (where symbols do have a physical meaning, because Plato said so).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly the fact that you tie the Orders to virtues in a bizarre, twisted fashion of Plato-inspired philosophy...works rather well for Mage, with it's pseudo-imperialism and patronizing separation of Sleeper beliefs and Awakened practices. This I can get behind. Justified nonsense is exactly the kind of thing I expect to see in a game about wizards with freeform magic and any half decent framework can generate interesting ideas here. If this is how they wishes to sell the Diamond Precept in this setting, I can buy it. </div> </div> </div>Happy you liked it! It was a sudden inspiration and I thought that it is something that the Diamond may indeed so in order to separate themselves from the Nameless.<br /> <br /> I hope it clarifies some thing, but if you have more criticisms/suggestions for improvement feel free to share, and waiting for your review of the rest of the section (notice that the Guardians and Mysterium are WIP).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T14:30:30-07:00","id":1514131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix853457</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513762-sorcerous-societies-new-revised-sects-orders?p=1514108#post1514108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Core Belief and Symbolism of the Forge of Vulcan and Watchers of Fortune in detail?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is hard to go too much in depth as it is not written (and this project already has more flesh than I intended), but in short-<br /> <br /> <b>Forge of Vulcan:</b> the Mercurian Manuscripts are texts comprising the philosophy of the Forge where everything can be described in terms of trade, transmutation and production, with magic being described as the resource which needs to be measured, calibrated and distributed. Think a philosophy which combines elements of economy and alchemy through the eyes of the producer, so a lot of &quot;law of equivalent exchange&quot;. Their Symbolism, Products, refers to them using tools which are both objects they personally crafted, the very act of manufacturing, bringing use to others through their actions, fair trade and work tools. Even giving charity to those in need or taking wealth from those who hoard it so it would bring use are part of their symbolism. A lot of focus about fulfilling the needs of the collective.<br /> <br /> <b>Watchers of Fortune:</b> the Will of the World is the idea that there is a &quot;natural way&quot; according to which things should happen, and that the Awakened most not disrupt that natural flow but work alongside of it. There is a lot of emphasis about &quot;being one with the world&quot; and not acting without understanding the consequences of your actions, and trying to align your own Will with that of the Supernal to make sure your actions serve the Truth, as the Supernal embodies itself within the Fallen and by reading the signs correctly one could fulfil their role and achieve Ascension. Their Symbolism, Patterns, focus around the idea that magic manifest itself through events which seems random, but hold meaning when looked at context. The flight of birds, the spilled entrails, the roll of dice- all of those are not random, but ways through which the Awakened can read the path they should take. That basically means OCD level of obsession in many regards, giving meaning for personal patterns and avoid actions until the events &quot;fit&quot;, as well as using astrology, geomancy and other methods which mean to &quot;balance&quot; or &quot;align&quot; the spell with the natural patterns of the world.<br /> <br /> Hope it helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T20:14:14-07:00","id":1514156,"title":"","content":"The watchtowers in <b>in the Forge of Vulcan</b>\u200b and watchers of fortune?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T22:26:57-07:00","id":1514164,"title":"","content":"Will the banisher section focus heavily on their 1st edition representation? I will be waiting for that one either way (banishers are an underrated antagonist in my opinion), but I would really like to know if you'd still discuss their newer incarnation as the Harrowed and such (since you have it typed in as an analysis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T23:39:02-07:00","id":1514170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513762-sorcerous-societies-new-revised-sects-orders?p=1514164#post1514164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the banisher section focus heavily on their 1st edition representation? I will be waiting for that one either way (banishers are an underrated antagonist in my opinion), but I would really like to know if you'd still discuss their newer incarnation as the Harrowed and such (since you have it typed in as an analysis</div> </div> </div> </div>Banishers are still way down the line, but it will be a combination, to a degree. Unlike other Sects, the Banishers will be more diverse, and the Harrowed will still be a phenomenon that is common among their Orders (even though it will be more common among some over others)<br /> <br /> Think about it in terms of how not every Seer have went through an Exarchal Awakening and not everyone with that form of Awakening becomes a Seer, but there is a strong correlation between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-08-2023, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T15:38:38-07:00","id":1514249,"title":"","content":"Finished the Guardians section in the document. Next is the Mysterium.","signatu